       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for adults, usually for inflammatory conditions\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily** (1,200\u20132,400 mg/day), common for pain or inflammation\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, if that was the intended daily amount. That could be 400 mg PO four times daily.\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm the dose you intended, and I'll enter it. If you really do need 1600 mg QID, please tell me the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note. That dose would probably also need pharmacist or attending review."
